So in production, config.git.baseBranch — is config.git always set? configLoader probably guarantees `config.git` exists with baseBranch default. Let me check configLoader defaults — if loadProjectConfig always populates config.git.baseBranch, then this latent crash never fires in production. My TEST should pass a config with git.baseBranch to exercise the real path (and the checkout mock throwing). And optionally add a test pinning the degraded behavior when config.git is missing: checkout is skipped entirely (TypeError caught) — behavior preserved by my refactor? In my refactor, `checkoutPrBranch(ctx, branchName)` → same expression `ctx.config.git.baseBranch` inside try → same TypeError → caught → warn. ✓ preserved as long as I keep the argument evaluation inside the try.

