Hmm — that clearly calls it. Unless... OH WAIT. I see it now! The mock pushes to `record.gitOps` — the record object captured in the closure... same object. Push + throw. The push MUST have happened.

Unless... the console output above shows the TAIL — the GITOPS line — and RESULT was on an earlier line. The entries start with getPRDiff — no checkout. So checkoutPRBranch was NEVER CALLED?!

Hmm wait — did `gitOps` in the module bind to my mock? The module requires './common/gitOps.js' — provided. `console.log('Checking out PR branch:'...)` — did that print? Let me check the full output — I tailed only 6 lines. If checkout had been called and thrown, we'd ALSO see `⚠️ Could not checkout PR branch: Error: local changes` warn line.

OH WAIT. I bet I know: **`config.git.baseBranch`** — accessing `.baseBranch` on undefined `config.git` THROWS inside the try! `config.git` is undefined in my debug config → `config.git.baseBranch` → TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'baseBranch') → caught by the try/catch → warn 'Could not checkout PR branch: TypeError...' — and the checkout call never happens (the argument evaluation threw BEFORE calling).

So in the CURRENT code, the console.log evaluates `config.workingDir || '(default)'` fine, then `gitOps.checkoutPRBranch(branchName, config.workingDir, config.git.baseBranch)` — config.git undefined → TypeError BEFORE invoking checkoutPRBranch — caught → warn → continue. That's the "2 entries" mystery: gitOps.checkoutPRBranch was never invoked; the catch logged a TypeError instead of my checkoutError!

So in production, config.git.baseBranch — is config.git always set? configLoader probably guarantees `config.git` exists with baseBranch default. Let me check configLoader defaults — if loadProjectConfig always populates config.git.baseBranch, then this latent crash never fires in production. My TEST should pass a config with git.baseBranch to exercise the real path (and the checkout mock throwing). And optionally add a test pinning the degraded behavior when config.git is missing: checkout is skipped entirely (TypeError caught) — behavior preserved by my refactor? In my refactor, `checkoutPrBranch(ctx, branchName)` → same expression `ctx.config.git.baseBranch` inside try → same TypeError → caught → warn. ✓ preserved as long as I keep the argument evaluation inside the try.

